namespace HdrPilot {
public static partial class Guide {
 static readonly Topic[] EnglishTopics={
 new Topic("HDR peak limit","Apply HDR in the UE5 method writes only Engine.ini and GameUserSettings.ini with backups. No ReShade, RenoDX, UE4SS or shader download is required. Apply HDR and Play game disable only the retired HDLSS_PeakLimit technique left by earlier builds, with transaction recovery. Other preset effects and mods are preserved. The peak is requested from the engine; the game may ignore or override it.","Requirements and verification","ReShade/RenoDX is managed separately and requires a compatible effect or game-specific mod. Switching the method does not install or remove components. Some mods require engine HDR; follow their documented setup to avoid two tone-mapping passes. The scene overlay works without either mod and reports captured pixel luminance. Engine CVars appear separately only with fresh UE4SS telemetry. Unavailable and stale data are explicitly identified. A software capture does not measure the physical panel."),
 new Topic("DLSS 5 control overlays","Install OptiScaler preserves the known DLSS 5 Swapper Overlay after verifying its SHA-256. This control panel is separate from the RenoDX Neural Rendering add-on.","Conflict checks","Unknown or modified DLSS/NR add-ons still require verification, even when their filename contains overlay. A separate RenoDX Neural Rendering add-on continues to block a second NR installation. Recognizing the control panel does not certify in-game compatibility."),
 new Topic("Getting started","The first launch uses English. A language selected on the home screen is saved for future launches. HDLSS helps configure HDR and community OptiScaler builds for installed games. Injection is performed through OptiScaler, ReShade or the game's engine settings, depending on your choice. HDLSS is independent of NVIDIA, Valve, Microsoft and the component authors.","Choose a game","Select a Steam or Xbox / Game Pass cover. The library is shared by the HDR and DLSS 5 sections. Covers grow with the window and keep the same size in both sections. The library uses a uniform background without game artwork. Sidebar commands use short labels on one line and the same font size. The home screen has two feature cards: Set up HDR and Set up DLSS 5. All previous component, version, rendering, restoration and shortcut choices remain in these sections. Overview returns to the two cards. Set up actions are at the top of each card so larger covers do not hide the main commands. Cover imports a JPG, PNG or BMP image for the selected game, including manually added games. A copy is stored in the app data folder and reused on restart. Prefer a high-resolution portrait image. Xbox artwork is selected from local package images by decoded resolution. All covers fill the same portrait area without distortion; wide images are cropped equally at both sides, keeping their center visible. The store label appears only below the artwork. Add game accepts an installed Windows game executable from any client. The entry is saved across restarts and launches that executable; the game may still require its client. Unsupported engine HDR remains unavailable. Back returns from HDR or DLSS 5 to the home cards. Help opens this guide. Diagnostics and Backups remain in the sidebar. Check the executable path: components are installed beside that executable. Use Executable and graphics to change the target or the expected graphics API.","Before applying changes","Close the game. Select the settings and review the file changes. Apply with backup writes the changes and keeps a recovery copy. Start the game from its launcher and verify the result. Installing a file does not prove it loaded in game.","Compatibility","The current app build targets Windows x64 and .NET Framework 4.8. Individual features have additional GPU, driver, game and display requirements. ARM64, 32-bit games and every hardware combination have not been certified. Protected installations and anti-cheat games may prevent modification."),
 new Topic("Installed or selected?","Yellow indicates a detected installed component or an explicitly applied setting read from game files. Blue indicates a selected choice that has not been applied. Saved preferences do not by themselves turn a choice yellow.","Components","ReShade and RenoDX buttons show installed status even for recognized files installed by another app. Stable/nightly or OptiScaler build identity is highlighted only when it can be verified. An unknown channel is not guessed from file presence.","Settings","DLSS 5 style, pass placement, pass count, loader and frame generation choices are compared with the installed configuration. HDR black level and output format distinguish values read from files from pending choices. Keep and missing defaults are not presented as explicitly applied. Applied does not mean measured or active in game."),
 new Topic("Engine HDR","Engine HDR is available for games where the required Unreal configuration has been identified. Other games can still use compatible ReShade effects or a supported RenoDX mod.","Brightness","Peak brightness is the requested highlight ceiling, not a guarantee that every scene reaches it. Midtones and interface brightness affect different parts of the image. Start with the monitor's calibrated values. Recommended fills in suggested values; Apply HDR saves them with backup.","Black level","The Unreal black parameter is logarithmic. Base Unreal uses -4; OLED near zero uses -6. These are tone-mapping references, not physical measurements of the display. Keep a custom value when a preset would overwrite your calibration.","Advanced output","scRGB uses a linear signal with Rec.709 primaries; HDR10 PQ uses Rec.2020. The 1000/2000 engine curves are presets, separate from your peak setting. Interface luminance, ACES scene multiplier, gamut compression and UI compositing affect supported engine paths. Turning off advanced editing preserves existing values."),
 new Topic("Monitor and live overlay","Select the display used by the game. EDID information is a starting point, not a physical measurement or a reading of Windows HDR calibration. If information is unavailable, enter your calibrated peak rather than assuming a value.","Scene luminance","Open live overlay analyzes captured HDR pixels. It reports a rounded scene peak, average and minimum, plus a recent history. It does not substitute saved settings or engine variables for scene measurements. The overlay region is excluded; the game's HUD may still be included. No screenshots are saved by this feature.","Capture format","scRGB in the overlay describes the Windows capture signal. A game configured for HDR10 can be captured through the Windows scRGB path. A scene peak below the configured limit is not by itself an error.","Shortcut and capture limits","Map the overlay shortcut in the HDR card or use HDR overlay key in HDR settings. Navigation keys can be used alone where supported. A reserved or occupied shortcut must be changed. Use borderless mode and keep the game in the foreground. Protected content or an unsupported capture path may prevent readings; use Overlay diagnostics to inspect the reason."),
 new Topic("UE4SS reader","The optional UE4SS reader reports engine parameters. It is separate from the live scene luminance overlay, which measures captured pixels.","Existing installations","Reader status distinguishes UE4SS, the HDLSS reader and whether the reader is enabled. Refresh reader status checks again. View engine parameters shows available telemetry. Old telemetry or a detected mod does not prove that the current game session is using it.","Installation and removal","Install UE4SS + reader downloads the official stable end-user package, shows the file plan and installs beside the real Unreal x64 executable. Existing UE4SS is preserved: Enable UE4SS reader adds only telemetry. Both flat and ue4ss subfolder layouts are detected. Custom override.txt, duplicate runtimes and occupied dwmapi.dll require manual review. Game-specific compatibility is not guaranteed: check a fresh UE4SS.log. Disable reader stops telemetry only. Recover operation with the saved transaction record reverses a new runtime installation. Manually added Unreal games are scanned from the game folder, including Engine/Plugins, for native DLSS SR/RR/FG updates. Missing DLLs do not mean the game supports those features."),
 new Topic("ReShade and RenoDX","In HDR, choose ReShade + RenoDX. Install ReShade with full add-on support, then install the RenoDX mod matched to the selected game. Adjust its HDR controls in the in-game ReShade menu.","Stable and nightly","Stable ReShade downloads the official stable package. Nightly uses a successful development build from the official repository's workflow. Both require full add-on support for RenoDX. Nightly can introduce regressions. The download is checked at installation time.","Game-specific mod","Install RenoDX resolves the game in the catalog and downloads a supported direct package when available. Follow the author's requirements. Some shared Unreal mods need engine HDR settings; the installer applies a supported documented recipe when one is identified. Unsupported or ambiguous packages must not be silently substituted.","Separate components","A pre-existing DLSS 5 add-on does not by itself block an HDR-only installation. ReShade can load through OptiScaler as ReShade64.dll, or through a supported direct loader. Unknown DLLs and duplicate loading paths are not overwritten. Uninstall ReShade, Restore RenoDX and the recovery controls remain separate."),
 new Topic("Nexus downloads","Some RenoDX mods are hosted on Nexus Mods rather than a direct release repository. A free account requires you to confirm the download on the website. HDLSS does not request your password.","Assisted flow","Keep the assistant window open, confirm the free download on Nexus and save the ZIP to the displayed folder. The app waits for the file to finish downloading, checks the archive and prepares the installation. Download folder lets you change the watched location.","Matching and limits","The supported flow expects the mod ID, RenoDX and the game's title in the original ZIP filename. A matching ZIP already in that folder can be used. Multiple matches, extra components or an unsupported archive format need review. A filename is not proof of origin. The supported ZIP contains one HDR RenoDX x64 add-on; package checks do not execute its code."),
 new Topic("Other ReShade effects","The effects catalog provides supported alternatives when a game has no suitable RenoDX mod. Effects have different purposes and do not all implement a correct HDR conversion.","Choosing an effect","Read the effect description and its requirements. AutoHDR, Lilium, Pumbo, qUINT and SweetFX entries must be used according to their supported package and effect type. Do not enable multiple competing HDR transformations by default.","Loading","Installing ReShade alone does not automatically enable shader effects. Configure the effect in the ReShade menu. An empty effect list is different from a failed ReShade installation. Add-ons and shader effects are separate."),
 new Topic("OptiScaler and DLSS 5","The DLSS 5 section uses community OptiScaler forks. These are not official NVIDIA injector builds. The build is downloaded from its author's repository when you install it.","Builds","Dagherbou, wilsjo2 and y4my4my4m provide different Neural Rendering paths. wilsjo2 exposes before-upscaling placement and multiple model passes. y4my4my4m has its own multipass and experimental MFG options. The actual release and capabilities must be verified per build and game.","GPU and driver","RTX 4000 and RTX 5000 use different NR compatibility paths. Detection and driver checks help select an appropriate runtime; choosing a series does not add hardware support. Experimental features must not be treated as universal compatibility.","Install or apply","Install OptiScaler downloads the selected build. Apply settings changes an existing installation and checks the required runtime. The preview lists changes before writing. ReShade HDR and engine settings are managed separately; do not add two competing NR injectors."),
 new Topic("Neural Rendering settings","Processing quality controls the model's input scale. Lower values can reduce GPU work; higher values process more detail. It does not change the desktop resolution. Compare the same scene when judging quality or speed.","Placement","Before upscaling runs the model before image enlargement and may process fewer pixels. After upscaling processes the enlarged image. The available behavior depends on the build. Keep leaves the existing configuration. Direct placement disables conflicting deferred or final-picture routing where that recipe is supported.","Passes and style","One pass is the starting point. Two or three passes repeat model processing, increasing cost and possibly artifacts; they do not generate extra frames. Style selects the model's artistic profile. Strength blends the model's result rather than changing HDR calibration."),
 new Topic("Frame Generation","Frame Generation creates intermediate frames. It differs from repeated Neural Rendering passes and does not multiply input responsiveness. Requested multipliers are not measured FPS.","Keep or change","Keep preserves existing FG settings. OptiScaler uses its own supported generation path. Game frame generation requests native FG settings and requires enabling the feature in the game. Disable OptiScaler FG affects the OptiScaler path; the game's own menu may still control native FG.","Multiplier and RTX 4000","The requested multiplier depends on the GPU, runtime, build and active DLSS-G pipeline. RTX 4000 above 2x is an experimental build-specific path, not standard guaranteed support. Do not interpret a configured multiplier or a detected DLL as evidence that MFG is running."),
 new Topic("DLLs and models","Installed components immediately lists Super Resolution, Ray Reconstruction, Frame Generation and the NR model, with detected versions or Not installed. The tooltip shows file paths. Check files and paths rescans the files and displays their paths. When several files exist for a component, the app compares SHA-256 hashes: identical files in multiple locations, different files to review, or an unavailable comparison. Multiple locations do not prove duplicate effects or a conflict. Identical files do not prove correct runtime loading or compatibility. Files are preserved; choose a component button to inspect or update one specific path. Backup folders are excluded from this inventory.","Four component buttons","Super Resolution, Ray Reconstruction, Frame Generation and Neural Rendering are grouped together. The first three open the respective DLL selector; Neural Rendering opens the model selector. They are different components and have independent restore controls.","Downloading versions","The DLL selector loads the latest ten catalog entries, selecting the most recent. Install selected version downloads and checks the package, NVIDIA signature, component identity and version. Latest from NVIDIA uses the NVIDIA repository. Catalog publication times can differ. Import DLL accepts a locally downloaded file, including a file obtained from the referenced TechPowerUp page.","What updates do not do","Replacing a DLL does not add SR, RR or FG support that the game does not implement. It does not unlock unsupported hardware. Model variants use their own repository and GPU compatibility checks. Identical DLL replacements are avoided."),
 new Topic("Uninstall and Steam originals","Uninstall / restore can remove HDLSS and a preceding recognized OptiScaler Autopilot installation in one reviewed operation. Available backups are restored. Unrelated HDR, UE4SS and other components remain separate.","Files and backups","Consumed Autopilot backups are moved into the app's recovery copy rather than left in the game folder. Conflicting backup copies stop the operation. The supported external manifest determines which files can be removed; unknown files and empty directories may remain.","Original game files","An external backup is not proof of an original Steam file. Verify Steam files asks Steam to check and recover the files it distributes. Verification does not replace removal of extra mod files. Without a valid backup or launcher verification, HDLSS cannot claim a fully original game folder.","Recovery","Recover operation uses the saved transaction record to undo a removal. Recovery stops if files have changed since the operation. Keep the data folder and its backups. A ReShade installation depending on the OptiScaler loader must be handled before that loader is removed."),
 new Topic("Activity and progress","The bottom area shows the current phase and a gold progress bar during component installation. Recent activity summarizes the main steps; Technical details opens the full log. Drag the activity area's handle to resize it.","Progress","Downloads and checks without a reliable total use an animated bar. File application reports completed files, not remaining time. Wait for completion before launching the game.","Interrupted operations","The app checks paths, source hashes and current files, then creates backups before applying changes. Supported write failures trigger rollback. If recovery cannot complete, keep the recovery folder and consult the technical details."),
 new Topic("Updates and preferences","English is the default for a new profile. Choose the language and appearance at the top right of the home screen. Monitor advice, file status and UE4SS reader status follow the selected language, including values and error messages. An explicitly saved language, theme, shortcut or per-game preference is retained when the app is updated.","Portable data","Replace the executable while preserving data. Adjacent HDR-Unlock folders can reuse an existing valid data folder through data-location.txt. Keep the older folder that actually contains those data. Backups and data opens the location in use.","Moving the app","When moving the app elsewhere, carry its data folder too. Detected game components can still be found without old preferences, but missing backups cannot be recreated. Divergent data stores are not silently merged.","Windows paths","The app enables .NET Framework long-path handling and declares long-path awareness to Windows. It does not change system registry policy. External tools and specific Windows configurations may have additional limits."),
 new Topic("Public release readiness","HDLSS is being prepared for public distribution. Version 1.0 introduces the HDLSS name. Existing HDR Unlock data and component records remain compatible. Successful tests on one PC do not establish compatibility with every configuration.","Validation","Test clean Windows profiles, different installation paths, GPU families, hybrid graphics, multiple displays, DPI settings, interrupted downloads and restore scenarios. Measure startup time, library scans, memory use, idle CPU and overlay cost before making performance claims.","Reporting an issue","Include the app version, Windows version, GPU and driver, game, selected executable, component versions and the relevant error. Review logs for personal paths before sharing them. Never send passwords or account keys.")
 };
}
}
